  - friction surface
  - landscape ecology
  - QGIS
  - Graphab
abstract: >-
  FricMaps is an open-source QGIS plugin that automates the production of
  standardised land-cover and resistance (friction) rasters for ecological
  connectivity modelling. It combines modular vector preprocessing with a
  rule-based rasterisation engine driven by a user-editable classification
  table. The workflow explicitly integrates underrepresented anthropogenic
  barriers such as fences, applies attribute-dependent buffering of roads and
  railways, and uses wildlife crossing structures to locally restore
  permeability at validated locations. It ingests French national datasets
  (BD TOPO, OCS GE, RPG, RGE ALTI) in both Shapefile and GeoPackage
  deliveries, supports user-defined custom data sources, and applies
  configurable multiplicative weighting rules. Outputs are ready for
  graph-based connectivity analysis, for instance with Graphab.
